{{Short description|Football tournament group stage}}
{{distinguish|1974 FIFA World Cup Group 2}}
{{more citations needed|date=January 2021}}
{{Use dmy dates|date=May 2018}}
Group B was one of two groups in the second group stage of the [[1974 FIFA World Cup]] finals. It was the first time that this stage of the competition (equivalent to the quarter-finals) was played in a group format.<ref>{{cite journal |last1=Csató |first1=László |last2=Kiss |first2=László Marcell |last3=Szádoczki |first3=Zsombor |title=The allocation of FIFA World Cup slots based on the ranking of confederations |journal=Annals of Operations Research |date=12 June 2024 |volume=344 |issue=1 |pages=153–173 |doi=10.1007/s10479-024-06091-5 |url=https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10479-024-06091-5 |language=en |issn=1572-9338}}</ref> Matches were played between 26 June and 3 July 1974 at venues in [[Düsseldorf]], [[Frankfurt]] and [[Stuttgart]]. Group B was made up of the winners of [[1974 FIFA World Cup Group 2|Groups 2]] and [[1974 FIFA World Cup Group 4|Groups 4]] ([[Yugoslavia national football team|Yugoslavia]] and [[Poland national football team|Poland]]), and the runners-up from [[1974 FIFA World Cup Group 1|Groups 1]] and [[1974 FIFA World Cup Group 3|Groups 3]] ([[Germany national football team|West Germany]] and [[Sweden men's national football team|Sweden]]).<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.rsssf.org/tables/74full.html |title=World Cup 1974 finals |publisher=[[RSSSF]] |access-date=30 April 2026}}</ref>

Having each won both of their first two matches, West Germany and Poland went into their final match level on points with a place in the [[1974 FIFA World Cup Final|final]] at stake. West Germany won the match 1–0 and qualified to play against the [[Netherlands national football team|Netherlands]], while Poland finished second and went on to play in the match for third place against [[Brazil national football team|Brazil]].<ref name="fifastudy">{{cite web |title=FIFA World Cup 1974 Final Competition Technical Study |url=http://www.fifa.com/mm/document/afdeveloping/technicaldevp/50/09/65/wc_74_tr_312.pdf |publisher=FIFA |access-date=3 March 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20111220060217/http://www.fifa.com/mm/document/afdeveloping/technicaldevp/50/09/65/wc%5f74%5ftr%5f312.pdf |archive-date=20 December 2011 |pages=57–62}}</ref>

==Qualified teams==
The winners of Group 2 and 4 and the runners-up of Group 1 and 3 qualified for Group B of the second round.

